WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.533
Here we are. They’re all ready, Fennekin!

2
00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.466
- Fenn!
- Ah!

3
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.266
These are traditional Pokémon sweet treats.

4
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:18.033
- They’re called Poké Puffs!
- Poké Puffs, huh?

5
00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:20.900
- Pika!
- Do you want one, Pikachu?

6
00:00:20.966 --> 00:00:23.866
- Pika. Pika.
- There you go!

7
00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:29.033
People can eat them too, right?

8
00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:33.266
-Oh!

9
00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:38.166
- Fenn?
- Ash, what’s the matter?

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.600
They’re great!

11
00:00:39.666 --> 00:00:42.800
That’s the yummiest thing I’ve ever eaten in my life!

12
00:00:42.866 --> 00:00:45.600
- Please don’t scare me like that..
- Na-na!

13
00:00:45.666 --> 00:00:48.566
- Can Dedenne have one?
- Sure!

14
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:57.133
Slurpuff!

15
00:00:57.199 --> 00:00:58.933
Huh? What?

16
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Ah!

17
00:01:01.066 --> 00:01:04.066
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

18
00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.466
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

19
00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:10.366
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

20
00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:13.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

21
00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:16.366
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

22
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:19.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

23
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:23.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

24
00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.433
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

25
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

26
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

27
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.199
Following Ash’s second Kalos Gym battle win in Cyllage City,

28
00:01:44.266 --> 00:01:47.833
our heroes are enjoying Serena’s fresh-baked Poké Puffs.

29
00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.233
Now, they seem to have company!

30
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.633
Slurpuff!

31
00:01:51.699 --> 00:01:54.033
No!

32
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.133
Slurpuff. The Meringue Pokémon.

33
00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:03.333
Slurpuff’s keen sense of smell is especially sensitive,

34
00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:05.866
much more than people’s.

35
00:02:05.933 --> 00:02:10.000
You see, Slurpuff thinks your Poké Puff tasted decent enough.

36
00:02:10.066 --> 00:02:14.066
Huh! What does that mean? Who are you?

37
00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.266
I’m Miette and this is my partner, Slurpuff.

38
00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:18.333
Slurpuff!

39
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.299
My name’s Ash. This is my partner, Pikachu!

40
00:02:21.366 --> 00:02:24.500
- Pikachu!
- And I’m Serena.

41
00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:26.633
- Clemont’s my name!
- I’m Bonnie.

42
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.033
Na-na-na!

43
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.866
Since my Slurpuff ate some of your Poké Puffs,

44
00:02:31.933 --> 00:02:33.666
how would you like to try some of the best?

45
00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:36.633
- Yes, please! I want one!
- Pika. Pika.

46
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.299
- I do, too!
- Thank you, but I’ll pass!

47
00:02:42.366 --> 00:02:45.299
Here you are! Enjoy!

48
00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:50.233
For Pikachu, a spicy Tamato Berry-topped Poké Puff.

49
00:02:50.299 --> 00:02:53.966
And a sweet Oren Berry-topped Poké Puff for Dedenne.

50
00:02:58.866 --> 00:03:01.066
- Pikachu!
- Na-na!

51
00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.233
I want to try that!

52
00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:05.433
Oh! Wait, but that’s...

53
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.466
Hot!

54
00:03:08.466 --> 00:03:11.600
Aw! That didn’t taste good. What was it?

55
00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:15.166
That was for Fire types! Poké Puffs are made for Pokémon,

56
00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.766
so they’re not all going to taste good to people!

57
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:19.100
Like that one.

58
00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:22.833
All Poké Puffs are baked with a particular Pokémon in mind.

59
00:03:22.899 --> 00:03:25.000
Hey, I make them like that, too!

60
00:03:25.066 --> 00:03:29.733
Course you can. That’s Poké Puff basics. Poké Puff 101.

61
00:03:29.799 --> 00:03:32.000
What’s with the attitude?

62
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:37.633
Calm down, you two! There’s no reason to be mad!

63
00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.733
Hm!

64
00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:41.533
- Uh...
- Why not have a bakeoff?

65
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.866
What was that, Bonnie?

66
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:46.600
There’s a Poké Puff Contest!

67
00:03:47.766 --> 00:03:50.899
The first round’s today and the final round’s tomorrow!

68
00:03:50.966 --> 00:03:53.000
- Great idea!
- Pika!

69
00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.200
I’ve never heard of a Poké Puff Contest.

70
00:03:55.266 --> 00:03:58.933
That's the reason I came here in the first place. I’m competing!

71
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.600
- We’ll see who the better chef is!
- Oh!!

72
00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:09.700
Now the preliminary round of the Poké Puff Contest

73
00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:11.399
is about to get under way!

74
00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:15.799
Contestants will compete using their own original Poké Puff recipes!

75
00:04:19.066 --> 00:04:22.733
I can hardly wait to see all the Poké Puffs!

76
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.333
Ta-da! The Poké Puff base layers are finished baking!

77
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.933
- Ha! They’re so fluffy!
- I could eat them just like they are!

78
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.533
- Pika.
- Now the next step.

79
00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:37.033
Two kinds of delicious frosting!

80
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.633
These frostings are my own original recipe and they’re delicious!

81
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.633
The topping goes on last!

82
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.233
A great baker has to have an eye for design.

83
00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.833
Fennekin!

84
00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.900
Ta-da! A Poké Puff topped with a small twig for Fennekin!

85
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.500
Hm. I’ll wipe the floor with her!

86
00:05:03.566 --> 00:05:05.533
All right, ladies and gentlemen,

87
00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:08.733
we’re now halfway through the preliminary round’s allotted time

88
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.000
and all our contestants are feverishly baking away!

89
00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.433
I’m seeing quite an amazing array of Poké Puffs!

90
00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.200
There’s a lot of skill on display this year.

91
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:25.133
Of course, there’s always an exception or two.

92
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:34.099
It’s time to announce the contestants who’ll be moving on to our final round!

93
00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:37.633
Joining us is Gena, world class Poké Puff Pâtissier

94
00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.266
and our Poké Puff Contest head judge!

95
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:42.933
Hidden inside each Poké Puff is one thing,

96
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.933
the hope that it will bring the hearts of people and Pokémon

97
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.033
closer together than ever before.

98
00:05:48.099 --> 00:05:51.599
An exquisite Poké Puff is certain to make the bond

99
00:05:51.666 --> 00:05:54.500
between Trainer and Pokémon even stronger!

100
00:05:55.566 --> 00:05:57.866
- Gena, excuse me!
- Huh? Oh.

101
00:05:58.866 --> 00:06:00.366
Huh?

102
00:06:00.433 --> 00:06:03.566
I need you to take care of my brother!

103
00:06:03.633 --> 00:06:05.099
Huh?

104
00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:08.866
Bonnie, I told you to stop this a million times!

105
00:06:08.933 --> 00:06:12.300
I hope you’ll think about it, please!

106
00:06:12.366 --> 00:06:16.400
Ignore her! This is so embarrassing!

107
00:06:18.299 --> 00:06:20.466
Take care of her brother, huh?

108
00:06:21.533 --> 00:06:25.333
So, Ash, do you already have someone to take care of you?

109
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.700
Huh? What are you talking about?

110
00:06:27.766 --> 00:06:29.433
Hm.

111
00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.166
Hm!

112
00:06:32.233 --> 00:06:34.833
I’m going to announce the three contestants

113
00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.900
who will move on to the final round.

114
00:06:36.966 --> 00:06:38.766
Only three of them? Wow!

115
00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:41.900
- I’m so nervous for you!
- Huh?

116
00:06:41.966 --> 00:06:45.466
Our first contestant is Miette!

117
00:06:45.533 --> 00:06:48.133
- Ha!
- No surprise.

118
00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.633
Next, the Berrybaker kids!

119
00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.700
- Huh?
- Huh? Big brother, we made it!

120
00:06:53.766 --> 00:06:56.966
All right! Let’s win with our sticky rice Poké Puffs!

121
00:06:58.433 --> 00:07:01.299
Finally, Serena!

122
00:07:01.366 --> 00:07:04.433
- Huh?
- All right!

123
00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.200
- You’re in!
- Serena, that’s wonderful!

124
00:07:07.266 --> 00:07:10.400
Thank you, but now it really begins!

125
00:07:15.433 --> 00:07:19.433
Our finalists are to come up with a new original Poké Puff recipe

126
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.966
by tomorrow’s round.

127
00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:25.033
They’ll also need to start gathering up the ingredients they’ll be using.

128
00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:29.833
That’s it! Onto the finals!

129
00:07:36.866 --> 00:07:39.533
Knocked out of the race at the starting gate.

130
00:07:39.599 --> 00:07:42.500
And now we won’t even get to execute our brilliant plan

131
00:07:42.566 --> 00:07:46.466
to catch every Pokémon we can find here after garnering the grand prize.

132
00:07:46.533 --> 00:07:48.833
Yeah. We blew it, but good.

133
00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:53.266
To think I was the Queen, the top Poké Puff chef for all of Team Rocket!

134
00:07:53.333 --> 00:07:56.466
- What’s she talking about?
- Beats the hat off of me!

135
00:07:56.533 --> 00:08:00.333
When it came to Poké Puffs, I was undefeated!

136
00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.433
The title of Poké Puff Queen will be mine forever!

137
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.599
Wobbuffet!

138
00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:09.533
If I can’t make my Poké Puffs, no one can!

139
00:08:10.966 --> 00:08:13.833
Do you have any berries left?

140
00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.366
Sorry. I’m completely sold out.

141
00:08:16.433 --> 00:08:19.166
-What do I do?

142
00:08:19.233 --> 00:08:21.833
I’m afraid you’ll have go to another shop.

143
00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:26.000
How can I bake Poké Puffs if I can’t find the right ingredients?

144
00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:31.666
Are they sold out, too?

145
00:08:31.733 --> 00:08:35.000
Every berry shop in town is out of berries!

146
00:08:35.066 --> 00:08:36.666
- Are you sure?
- Uh!

147
00:08:36.733 --> 00:08:39.400
I wonder if this is on purpose.

148
00:08:39.466 --> 00:08:41.766
Is this your fault?

149
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:44.366
Why would I do such a thing?

150
00:08:44.433 --> 00:08:46.566
Maybe the forest will have berries!

151
00:08:46.633 --> 00:08:48.533
Na-na-na!

152
00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.733
Good idea! Let’s all go to the forest and look!

153
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.133
- Pika. Pika.
- Yeah! Let’s go look!

154
00:08:55.199 --> 00:08:58.133
Hm!

155
00:09:03.766 --> 00:09:06.300
- I don’t see any.
- Pika.

156
00:09:06.366 --> 00:09:08.433
But how can that be?

157
00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.800
This wasn’t from natural causes.

158
00:09:10.866 --> 00:09:13.033
Someone’s sabotaging the contest.

159
00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.966
Who would do such a bad thing?

160
00:09:15.033 --> 00:09:16.166
Na-na-na-na!

161
00:09:16.233 --> 00:09:17.566
I wonder...

162
00:09:17.633 --> 00:09:19.933
I’ll go see if I can find something!

163
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.333
Fennekin!

164
00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.166
- Serena!
- Pika.

165
00:09:23.233 --> 00:09:25.300
Being frantic isn’t going to help.

166
00:09:25.366 --> 00:09:27.666
I guess. You have any ideas, Miette?

167
00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.633
My Slurpuff can help figure this thing out!

168
00:09:30.699 --> 00:09:34.366
If something sweet’s in the air, Slurpuff can find where it is.

169
00:09:34.433 --> 00:09:37.100
So finding berries should be a piece of cake!

170
00:09:37.166 --> 00:09:39.333
- Slurpuff.
- Will you do that for us?

171
00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.233
Slurpuff. Slurpuff.

172
00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.800
Slurpuff, Slurpuff.

173
00:09:44.866 --> 00:09:47.033
It says there are berries this way!

174
00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.100
- Wow! Awesome!
- Pika!

175
00:09:49.166 --> 00:09:50.466
- Huh?

176
00:09:50.533 --> 00:09:52.033
That was Serena!

177
00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:56.800
- Help me!
- Serena!

178
00:10:04.966 --> 00:10:08.100
Come on! What do you want?

179
00:10:08.166 --> 00:10:11.033
Slur!

180
00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.199
Who’s that Pokémon?

181
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.166
It’s Slurpuff!

182
00:10:24.733 --> 00:10:26.900
Please, stay away!

183
00:10:26.966 --> 00:10:30.633
Oh! argh!

184
00:10:30.699 --> 00:10:33.166
- Fennekin, use Scratch, quick!
- Fennekin!

185
00:10:33.233 --> 00:10:36.366
Yah!

186
00:10:36.433 --> 00:10:39.199
Oh! Fennekin!

187
00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.000
Oh, Serena! Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!

188
00:10:45.066 --> 00:10:48.566
Pika! Pikachu!

189
00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.633
- Oh!
- Fenn!

190
00:10:52.699 --> 00:10:55.166
- You okay?
- Yeah, I’m fine.

191
00:10:55.233 --> 00:10:58.133
-All right, who’s that Pokémon?

192
00:10:59.633 --> 00:11:02.400
Swirlix, the Cotton Candy Pokémon.

193
00:11:02.466 --> 00:11:06.533
Swirlix only eats sweets, making its fur as sticky as cotton candy.

194
00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.766
- They’re so cute.
- Ah. Maybe, but now they’re really mad.

195
00:11:15.033 --> 00:11:17.733
How dare you suddenly attack us like that?

196
00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.100
Fennekin, use Flamethrower.

197
00:11:20.166 --> 00:11:23.466
Fennekin!

198
00:11:28.866 --> 00:11:31.400
Huh? Why’d they attack you?

199
00:11:31.466 --> 00:11:34.233
It’s your fault for letting your guard down.

200
00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:39.199
Hm! I’m all sticky. That’s why there aren’t any berries in the forest.

201
00:11:39.266 --> 00:11:43.033
- The Swirlix must have eaten all of them.
- Slurpuff! Slurpuff!

202
00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:46.833
- That’s not what Slurpuff thinks.
- Well, how would it know?

203
00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:51.300
Slurpuff evolves from Swirlix, so it knows how they behave.

204
00:11:51.366 --> 00:11:55.833
Then that must mean the Swirlix were angry about something else.

205
00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.033
Slurpuff! Slurpuff! Slur!

206
00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.500
- It’s telling us to follow.
- Let’s go.

207
00:12:05.566 --> 00:12:09.800
Huh? It must have smelled something.

208
00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.033
Huh?

209
00:12:19.033 --> 00:12:20.800
It’s a dead-end.

210
00:12:20.866 --> 00:12:24.133
- How are we going to get over that?
- Na-na.

211
00:12:24.199 --> 00:12:26.533
Hm. Uh!

212
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:31.666
Hey, I know. We’ll all be able to climb that cliff if we work together as a team.

213
00:12:31.733 --> 00:12:34.666
- Clemont, ask Chespin to come out.
- I understand.

214
00:12:34.733 --> 00:12:37.599
Now, Chespin, let’s go.

215
00:12:37.666 --> 00:12:38.733
Chespin!

216
00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:42.466
- It’s your turn.
- Right. Slurpuff, help us out.

217
00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:52.066
Okay, Chespin, use Vine Whip and lift us all up there.

218
00:12:52.133 --> 00:12:54.166
Pin! Pin! Chespin! Pin!

219
00:12:55.633 --> 00:12:58.733
Pika. Pika!

220
00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.800
Pika! Pika!

221
00:13:04.866 --> 00:13:07.800
-All right. Awesome job!

222
00:13:14.366 --> 00:13:15.833
Thanks, Clemont.

223
00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.033
- Chespin, you’re amazing.
- Pin! Che!

224
00:13:19.099 --> 00:13:21.933
You were a big help. Thanks, Chespin.

225
00:13:22.933 --> 00:13:26.199
- Oh, wow!
- Huh? Look at that.

226
00:13:26.266 --> 00:13:28.266
Lots of berry trees.

227
00:13:28.333 --> 00:13:33.199
- I can’t believe how many there are.
- Millions.

228
00:13:35.633 --> 00:13:38.333
I’ll make amazing Poké Puffs with these.

229
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.699
- They’re delicious.
- Pika, Pikachu.

230
00:13:40.766 --> 00:13:42.266
Already?

231
00:13:42.333 --> 00:13:44.199
Slurpuff! Slurpuff! Slur!

232
00:13:44.266 --> 00:13:47.133
- What, Slurpuff?
- Slur. Slurpuff.

233
00:13:51.199 --> 00:13:55.033
- Oh, no, not them again!
- Something else is going on.

234
00:13:58.599 --> 00:14:04.333
What’s that?

235
00:14:11.366 --> 00:14:12.699
You!

236
00:14:12.766 --> 00:14:15.333
Prepare for trouble, who else would it be?

237
00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.699
And make it double, the same goes for me.

238
00:14:17.766 --> 00:14:20.199
To protect the world from devastation.

239
00:14:20.266 --> 00:14:22.966
To unite all people within our nation.

240
00:14:23.033 --> 00:14:25.900
To denounce the evils of bad cuisine.

241
00:14:25.966 --> 00:14:28.699
To extend our reach to the big berry scene.

242
00:14:28.766 --> 00:14:31.266
- Jessie!
- And James!

243
00:14:31.333 --> 00:14:34.366
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

244
00:14:34.433 --> 00:14:37.566
Surrender now or prepare for a frantic food fight.

245
00:14:37.633 --> 00:14:39.133
Meowth, that’s right.

246
00:14:39.199 --> 00:14:40.866
Wobbuffet!

247
00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.066
Who’s that?

248
00:14:45.133 --> 00:14:46.633
- Team Rocket!
- Pika.

249
00:14:46.699 --> 00:14:51.433
We’re taking over the berry business. It’s all ours as far as the eye can see.

250
00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.300
Which means your twerpish baking days are over.

251
00:14:54.366 --> 00:14:56.566
And while we’re at it, we’ll grab all of your Pokémon

252
00:14:56.633 --> 00:14:58.633
and leave you with a big windbag full of air.

253
00:14:58.699 --> 00:15:00.766
- Why you...
- Pika, Pika!

254
00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:03.766
It's no wonder we couldn’t find a single berry anywhere.

255
00:15:03.833 --> 00:15:06.366
Now I understand why the Swirlix were so angry.

256
00:15:06.433 --> 00:15:09.433
Huh! Knowing the truth won’t set you free.

257
00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:12.266
- Show them a thing or three.
- Leave it to me.

258
00:15:12.333 --> 00:15:15.533
Check out my Robo Baby Buggy Berry-Robbing Swipe the Sweets

259
00:15:15.599 --> 00:15:18.266
and Make Our Own Treats Octillery Mark Three.

260
00:15:18.333 --> 00:15:21.133
Huh? That's such a creative name.

261
00:15:21.199 --> 00:15:23.500
- You would think that.
- Ouch.

262
00:15:23.566 --> 00:15:27.099
On the Pokémon side of things, we’ll grab Pikachu first.

263
00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:32.033
-Pika!

264
00:15:32.099 --> 00:15:34.400
- Pikachu.
- Pika!

265
00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:37.366
- Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

266
00:15:37.433 --> 00:15:40.866
Sorry. This machine is guaranteed Thunderbolt resistant.

267
00:15:40.933 --> 00:15:43.366
Now for the rest of the twerp’s Pokémon.

268
00:15:43.433 --> 00:15:47.366
Pika! Pika!

269
00:15:47.433 --> 00:15:49.000
Turn it up to ten!

270
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.099
No, Swirlix.

271
00:15:56.433 --> 00:16:01.666
How sweet it is! Swimming in a sea of sweet success. Yes!

272
00:16:01.733 --> 00:16:04.266
- Oh, the shame. Just kidding!
- Yup.

273
00:16:04.333 --> 00:16:08.133
We’re just a-sailing along 'cause we’re strong!

274
00:16:08.199 --> 00:16:10.500
Wobbuffet!

275
00:16:10.566 --> 00:16:14.500
Pikachu and Swirlix! What can I do?

276
00:16:14.566 --> 00:16:17.933
Hey, Clemont! Does their machine have any weak spot?

277
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.666
- Weak spot? Let’s see.
- Hurry up.

278
00:16:20.733 --> 00:16:23.800
Okay. First off, it’s a giant vacuum.

279
00:16:23.866 --> 00:16:26.733
It has to suck in air in order to function.

280
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.800
I’ve got it! Seal their suction tube.

281
00:16:29.866 --> 00:16:33.733
- That will definitely stop the airflow.
- Great idea. I’m going!

282
00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.433
- Stop the twerp in his tracks!
- We’re really cleaning up!

283
00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:44.233
You can’t stop me!

284
00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.633
What, are you, nuts?

285
00:16:50.633 --> 00:16:53.566
Hang on! I promise I’ll get you guys out of there.

286
00:16:53.633 --> 00:16:56.199
- Ash, no!
- Oh, wow, Ash is so brave!

287
00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:58.666
- Careful, Ash!
- You can do it, Ash!

288
00:17:00.133 --> 00:17:01.333
Huh?

289
00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:05.833
Now’s your chance! Get out of there!

290
00:17:05.899 --> 00:17:07.566
Pika. Pika.

291
00:17:07.633 --> 00:17:10.466
Pikachu, Swirlix!

292
00:17:10.533 --> 00:17:14.566
The engine overheated. That stopped the machine. We should attack now.

293
00:17:14.633 --> 00:17:18.500
- Fennekin, Flamethrower, go!
- Fenn!

294
00:17:23.133 --> 00:17:27.700
- This could be a little bit of a problem.
- Little? We’re going to explode.

295
00:17:27.766 --> 00:17:30.066
Cut the small talk and do something.

296
00:17:30.133 --> 00:17:32.166
Switching to exhaust!

297
00:17:32.233 --> 00:17:33.833
Huh?

298
00:17:37.899 --> 00:17:40.833
Ow! Huh?

299
00:17:40.899 --> 00:17:42.266
Pika!

300
00:17:42.333 --> 00:17:45.266
You okay, Pikachu?

301
00:17:45.333 --> 00:17:49.433
Pikachu, Swirlix, you okay? Snap out of it.

302
00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.433
Pika! Pi!

303
00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:57.233
Uh! That's great. Swirlix. I need you to help me out by stopping that machine.

304
00:18:04.533 --> 00:18:07.300
Leave us alone!

305
00:18:07.366 --> 00:18:08.399
That's awesome!

306
00:18:08.466 --> 00:18:10.800
Hey, Slurpuff! Why don’t we help them out too?

307
00:18:10.866 --> 00:18:12.366
Slurpuff!

308
00:18:12.433 --> 00:18:14.600
Fennekin, use Flamethrower!

309
00:18:14.666 --> 00:18:16.233
Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!

310
00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.333
Slurpuff, use Energy Ball!

311
00:18:18.399 --> 00:18:19.966
- Fennekin!
- Pikachu!

312
00:18:20.033 --> 00:18:22.200
Slurpuff!

313
00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.600
- I still bake the best.
- We’re all cooked.

314
00:18:28.666 --> 00:18:30.566
Time to cool off.

315
00:18:30.633 --> 00:18:33.533
There’s nothing sweet about blasting off.

316
00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:34.466
Wobbuff!

317
00:18:34.533 --> 00:18:35.866
- And we’re doing...
- It...

318
00:18:35.933 --> 00:18:39.466
- Again.
- Wobbuffet!

319
00:18:45.266 --> 00:18:49.966
And now, we’ll announce the winner of our fabulous Poké Puff Contest.

320
00:18:50.033 --> 00:18:53.166
Presenting our head judge, Gena. Take it away.

321
00:18:55.033 --> 00:18:58.833
The Berrybaker kids incorporated exotic flavors into their Poké Puff,

322
00:18:58.899 --> 00:19:02.600
creating a delicacy that is comforting and innovative.

323
00:19:02.666 --> 00:19:05.366
Using Passho Berry for her Poké Puff topping,

324
00:19:05.433 --> 00:19:09.033
Serena has created a delight with flavor and a hint of heat.

325
00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.766
Fire types are sure to love her Poké Puff.

326
00:19:11.833 --> 00:19:16.399
And finally, Miette’s Poké Puff is made with cotton candy and whipped cream

327
00:19:16.466 --> 00:19:18.333
and topped with a Tamato Berry.

328
00:19:18.399 --> 00:19:23.600
Both Electric-type and Fairy-type Pokémon are certain to love this presentation.

329
00:19:26.666 --> 00:19:29.600
And now, the winner is...

330
00:19:34.266 --> 00:19:36.566
I’m happy to announce...

331
00:19:38.966 --> 00:19:40.966
The Berrybaker kids win it!

332
00:19:42.366 --> 00:19:48.200
Yes! Berrybakers rule.

333
00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.800
- I’m sorry Serena and Miette both lost.
- Na-na!

334
00:19:55.866 --> 00:19:57.700
There’s always next time.

335
00:20:00.766 --> 00:20:02.700
So where are you going from here?

336
00:20:02.766 --> 00:20:05.700
I'm headed anywhere that helps me make better Poké Puffs.

337
00:20:05.766 --> 00:20:09.133
Next time I see you, my Poké Puffs will be even tastier.

338
00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.366
Mine, too.

339
00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.966
Maybe this was all for the best.

340
00:20:17.033 --> 00:20:19.033
- Yeah.
- Pikachu.

341
00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:21.033
Serena, got to go!

342
00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.866
Huh?

343
00:20:22.933 --> 00:20:23.933
Take care.

344
00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.633
- One thing.
- Huh?

345
00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:30.399
Either you tell Ash how you feel about him or I’ll tell him how I feel.

346
00:20:30.466 --> 00:20:32.966
- Huh!
- Don’t say I didn’t warn you.

347
00:20:33.033 --> 00:20:35.566
Hm! Huh!

348
00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.899
Poké Puffs make everyone happy,

349
00:20:38.966 --> 00:20:42.300
not to mention bring together people with a love for baking.

350
00:20:42.366 --> 00:20:45.266
Now our heroes are off to Shalour City once again,

351
00:20:45.333 --> 00:20:47.866
as the journey continues.
